            <ArticleTitle>Spectrum of clinical manifestations of West Nile virus infection in children.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1673-5</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Reports of clinical manifestations of West Nile virus (WNV) infections in children have been relatively rare. Four cases of WNV infection in children are described: the first report of prolonged encephalitis and fulminant hepatitis caused by WNV, and 3 other presentations of WNV, including the first report of ocular involvement in a child.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
